-- title:
--   Tame inertia at supersingular points: cyclic, order prime to p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, together with the tameness conditions that either $p\neq 2$ or some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv 1 \pmod 4$, and that if $p=3$ then some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv 1\pmod 3$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ let $K_1$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142) (the $\mathbb{Q}$-field generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$) and $K_2$ the one generated by that for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$, with $K_2\le K_1$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and with compatible algebra structures on $K_1$ and $K_2$. Let $j\in K_1$ and $j_2\in K_2$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent series are both the base-changed $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Consider the two-chart integral models over $A$, pushouts of the spectra of the chart algebras of elements integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$, and a morphism $\pi_2$ from the model of $(K_1,j)$ to that of $(K_2,j_2)$, together with an $A$-algebra map $\iota_{F_2}$ of finite-chart algebras inducing the inclusion of Laurent series; it is assumed that $\pi_2$ is compatible with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with the finite-chart immersions, that the preimage under $\pi_2$ of the finite chart is the finite chart, that $\pi_2$ and $\iota_{F_2}$ are finite, and that membership in the finite chart algebra of $K_1$ is equivalent to integrality over the image of $\iota_{F_2}$. Let $z$ be a point of the model of $(K_1,j)$ at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and $y$ a point of the finite chart mapping to $z$ such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Finally let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully by semiring automorphisms on $K_1$, acting trivially on the elements whose Laurent series lie in $K_2$ and with invariants exactly those elements, and acting on the finite chart algebra compatibly with its action on $K_1$. Then for $\mathfrak{y}$ the prime ideal of $y$, the inertia subgroup $\mathfrak{y}.\mathrm{inertia}\ G$ is cyclic and its cardinality is not divisible by $p$.
--
--   This is the tame-level statement that the automorphism (diamond) inertia group at a supersingular point of the special fibre of the integral model attached to $X_1(M)\cap X_0(p)$ over the $X_0(Mp)$-level is cyclic of order prime to $p$, reflecting that $\mathrm{Aut}(E_0,C_M)/\pm 1$ embeds in $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ once wild automorphisms at $p=2,3$ are excluded by the congruence conditions on divisors of $M$. It feeds the local description of the completed stalks of the crossing model at supersingular points.
